          <h2 class="title is-2 mt-2 mb-4">Raja Swarnil Singhai</h2>
          <div class="content is-medium about-story__text">
            <p>
              I've been working in the Salesforce ecosystem for <strong>7 years in India</strong> — building, breaking, fixing, and occasionally crying over data transforms in CRM Analytics.
            </p>
            <p>
              My core expertise is <strong>CRM Analytics (CRMA)</strong> — dashboards, datasets, recipes, dataflows, and the dark art of making Einstein Analytics do exactly what a stakeholder described in a 47-word voice note at 11pm.
            </p>
            <p>
              Now I'm heading to <strong>Europe as a CRMA Engineer</strong>, and I built this platform so that everything I know — and everything I'm still learning — lives somewhere structured, useful, and accessible to anyone.
            </p>
            <p>
              This isn't a personal blog that drifted into a course platform. It was designed from the start as a proper <strong>open-source LMS</strong> for Salesforce people who want to learn AI, analytics, development, and architecture the right way.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="about-story__social buttons mt-5">
